{"type":"text","timestamp":1782045356667,"sessionID":"ses_115d46e78ffePbz2OLggcEL3CT","part":{"id":"prt_eea2e29090015CuQAGfCmP2e5N","messageID":"msg_eea2e1b780012r5xVb0bdU2MDU","sessionID":"ses_115d46e78ffePbz2OLggcEL3CT","type":"text","text":"Done. Implemented a Javalin + SQLite REST API for managing books.\n\n**Files created:**\n- `pom.xml` — Maven build (Javalin 6.3.0, sqlite-jdbc, Jackson, JUnit 5, OkHttp)\n- `src/main/java/com/example/books/Book.java` — record model\n- `src/main/java/com/example/books/ValidationException.java`\n- `src/main/java/com/example/books/BookRepository.java` — JDBC CRUD against SQLite\n- `src/main/java/com/example/books/BookController.java` — route handlers + validation (title/author required)\n- `src/main/java/com/example/books/Main.java` — Javalin wiring, exception handlers, `main`\n- `src/test/java/com/example/books/BookApiIntegrationTest.java` — 6 integration tests (boots the full app against a temp SQLite DB)\n- `README.md` — setup/run/endpoint docs\n\n**Endpoints:** `GET /health`, `POST /books`, `GET /books` (with `?author=`), `GET/PUT/DELETE /books/{id}` with appropriate status codes (200/201/204/400/404/500).\n\n**Build result:** `Tests run: 6, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0` — `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nRun with `mvn clean package && java -jar target/book-api-1.0.0.jar`.","time":{"start":1782045354249,"end":1782045356665}}}
